# Reverse proxy in front of the API on the Hetzner box (#13). Mounted read-only
# by the `caddy` service in compose.prod.yml; API_DOMAIN comes from the host
# .env through that service's environment.
#
# TLS: a Cloudflare ORIGIN CA certificate, with the zone's SSL mode set to
# "Full (strict)". Two alternatives were rejected:
#   - plain HTTP on 80 + Cloudflare "Flexible": OTP codes and JWTs would cross
#     the public internet Cloudflare → Hetzner in the clear on every request;
#   - Let's Encrypt via ACME: the HTTP-01 challenge has to pass through the
#     proxy's own redirect rules ("Always Use HTTPS"), which is fragile, and
#     buys nothing here — the only client that ever reaches this port is
#     Cloudflare, and the origin cert (free, 15-year) is trusted by exactly it.
# Files: ./certs/origin.pem and ./certs/origin.key on the box (runbook §2.3).
# Port 80 stays open: with a `tls` block Caddy still redirects http → https.
#
# No `header_up Upgrade` / `Connection`: Caddy v2 proxies WebSockets
# (Socket.IO's transport) automatically. Hand-written upgrade headers break it.

{$API_DOMAIN} {
	tls /certs/origin.pem /certs/origin.key
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy api:3001
}
